   "replyText": "That's a good start, and the picture on the screen shows a big hot sun, which matches your sentence nicely.\n\nNow let's build it up. If the sun is hot, what do we feel on our skin when we stand outside? Try finishing this: \"The sun is hot, so...\""
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "text": "The moon is white.",
   "startT": 23941,
   "endT": 26358,
   "audioSec": 2.42,
   "replyAudioLatencyMs": 2298,
   "replyTextEventLatencyMs": 2143,
   "heard": "The moon is white.",
   "heardMessages": 1,
   "transcriptLatencyMs": 163,
   "queries": [
    {
     "status": 200,
     "firstContentMs": 1342,
     "totalMs": 2135,
     "chars": 202
    }
   ],
   "replyText": "Nice sentence, and you used \"is\" correctly again. Now, keeping the same pattern, try adding \"and\" to make it longer. So say it like this: \"The moon is white and...\" What else can you say about the moon?"
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "text": "I can see the stars.",
   "startT": 42882,
   "endT": 45575,
   "audioSec": 2.69,
   "replyAudioLatencyMs": 2401,
   "replyTextEventLatencyMs": 2245,
   "heard": "I can see the stars.",
   "heardMessages": 1,
   "transcriptLatencyMs": -174,
   "queries": [
    {
     "status": 200,
     "firstContentMs": 1760,
     "totalMs": 2550,
     "chars": 159
    }
   ],
   "replyText": "That's a lovely sentence, and you used \"can see\" perfectly. Look at the screen and pick one star. Now tell me what colour it is, starting with \"The star is...\""
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "text": "The sky is dark at night.",
   "startT": 60699,
   "endT": 63720,
   "audioSec": 3.02,
   "replyAudioLatencyMs": 2136,
   "replyTextEventLatencyMs": 1980,
   "heard": "The sky is dark at night.",
   "heardMessages": 1,
   "transcriptLatencyMs": 1,
   "queries": [
    {
     "status": 200,
     "firstContentMs": 1430,
     "totalMs": 2251,
     "chars": 214
    }
   ],
   "replyText": "Yes, that's right, and it's a great sentence because it joins two ideas with a clear reason.\n\nNow let's keep practising. Finish this one for me: \"The sky is dark at night, so I can see...\" What do you see up there?"
  }
